B.aj9=new A.j8("What stays on your device","Your settings, bookmarks, progress, reflections, saved Hadi conversations and any AI key you enter are stored on your device. You can clear them by clearing the app's data or by removing the key in Hadi settings.")
B.aj6=new A.j8("Hadi and AI providers","Hadi can answer from an offline library that never leaves your device. If you add your own key for an AI provider (for example Groq, OpenRouter or xAI), your key and the messages in your conversation are sent to that provider to produce an answer, under their terms and privacy policy. Messages that look like a personal crisis are answered on the device and are not sent to any provider or saved.")
B.aj2=new A.j8("Your account","If you create an account we use Firebase Authentication (Google) to store your name, email address and sign-in method. Deleting your account removes the sign-in record and the account data we keep about you.")
B.aj3=new A.j8("The Majlis","What you post in the Majlis (title, text, display name and an identifier for your account) is stored in Firebase Firestore and is public. Deleting your account does not automatically remove posts already published; contact us to ask for a post to be removed.")
B.aj5=new A.j8("Location and other services","Prayer times, Qibla and the mosque finder use the location you give or allow. The app contacts third-party services to work: prayer time and map services, audio servers for recitation, and GitHub to download updated content (this reveals your IP address to that service). Each has its own privacy policy.")
B.aja=new A.j8("We do not sell your data","We do not sell personal data or show advertising based on it.")
B.aj7=new A.j8("Your choices","You can delete your account from the Delete account screen, clear local data from your device settings, and ask us about any data we hold about you at the contact address [to be added by the app owner before public release].")
B.ajc=new A.j8("Children and the Family Wing","Ar-Rayaan is a general-audience app. It is not directed to children under 13 (or the age of digital consent where you live), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from a child. The Family Wing lets a parent or guardian set up learning profiles for the children in their care; the parent is the person who uses the app and who gives consent.\n\nWhat a profile holds. For each child a parent adds, the app keeps on the device: a first name or nickname chosen by the parent (limited to 30 characters), the date the profile was created, and the child\u2019s progress in the School of Letters (lessons finished, exam scores, mastery marks). We do not ask for or store a child\u2019s age, date of birth, photo, voice, email address, phone number or location.\n\nWhere it is kept. Child profiles and progress are stored only on the device, in the app\u2019s local storage. They are not sent to our servers or to any third party. A child\u2019s name is never included in any request to an AI service or to Firebase. Cloud sync of family data is switched off; if we ever offer it, it will be optional, will need a parent\u2019s separate consent first, and will never include a child\u2019s name.\n\nWasia and AI services. When a child uses Wasia, answers come from the app\u2019s own lesson content. Only if a parent turns on \u201cAsk the AI service\u201d for children is a child\u2019s question sent to the AI service the app is connected to (the parent\u2019s own key, or one managed with their subscription; for example Groq, OpenRouter or xAI), without the child\u2019s name and without other profile data. Parents can turn this off at any time.\n\nConsent and parental controls. Before a first profile is created the parent confirms that they are the child\u2019s parent or guardian and agrees to this section. Adding or removing a child, and the AI setting for children, sit behind a parent check. A parent can delete a single child or all children at any time; deletion removes the name and all progress from the device immediately, and withdraws the stored consent.\n\nRetention. Profiles and progress are kept until the parent deletes them or the app is uninstalled, whichever comes first. Because the data is only on the device, we cannot retrieve it for you and do not hold a copy.\n\nAdvertising and analytics. The app contains no advertising and no analytics or crash-reporting service that receives information about children.\n\nContact. If you believe a child has given us personal information, or you have questions about this section, contact us using the address in the Terms and Privacy screens and we will help you delete it.\n")
B.aqA=s([B.aj9,B.aj6,B.aj2,B.aj3,B.aj5,B.aja,B.aj7,B.ajc],t.J8)
B.bky=new A.WS("Privacy Policy",B.aqA,null)
B.aj1=new A.j8("What Ar-Rayaan is","Ar-Rayaan is a study and reflection companion: Qur'an, hadith, supplications, prayer-time tools, learning material and stories. It is not a religious authority.")
B.aje=new A.j8("Not a source of fatwa","Nothing in the app, including answers from Hadi, the Majlis or any calculator, is a fatwa or a ruling for your situation. For rulings on worship, family, finance, health or any personal matter, ask a qualified scholar. Calculated prayer times and Zakat amounts are aids; check them against your local mosque or scholar.")
B.ajf=new A.j8("Not medical, mental-health or emergency help","The app is not a medical or counselling service. If you or someone else is in danger, contact your local emergency number or a crisis line straight away. Sakina lists help lines by country, but the app cannot call for help on your behalf.")
B.ajd=new A.j8("Your account","You are responsible for what you do with your account and for keeping your password private. You can delete your account at any time from the Delete account screen.")
B.aj8=new A.j8("The Majlis (community)","Posts in the Majlis are public and shown with the display name you choose. They are not reviewed before they appear. Do not post anything unlawful, abusive, hateful, deceptive, or that shares private information about other people, and do not claim to be Ar-Rayaan, its staff or a scholar. Posts can be reported and may be removed. You are responsible for what you post.")
B.aj4=new A.j8("Content and accuracy","We work to keep Qur'an, hadith and other religious content accurate and to cite sources, but errors can occur. If you find one, please tell us so it can be corrected.")
B.ajb=new A.j8("Changes and contact","These terms may change; the version shown here is the one that applies. Contact address: [to be added by the app owner before public release].")
B.az7=s([B.aj1,B.aje,B.ajf,B.ajd,B.aj8,B.aj4,B.ajb],t.J8)
B.bkz=new A.WS("Terms of Service",B.az7,null)
